  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Y&#x2019;en a Marre (&#x201C;We are fed up&#x201D; or &#x201C;Enough is Enough&#x201D;) was initiated as a popular citizen movement against injustice and inequality in Senegal in January 2011 by a collective of rappers, artists, journalists, students, intellectuals, and members of other socio-professional groups. Y&#x2019;en a Marre is an experienced grassroots national network working on diverse topics including citizenship, citizen participation, transparency in public affairs management, and youth and women&#x2019;s leadership. It has focused on mobilizing citizens, especially young people to convince government authorities to consider the people&#x2019;s priorities as their own. This grant will allow Y&#x2019;en a Marre to develop its strategic plan for the next 5 years, restructure its operations and programs and develop its resource mobilization and monitoring and evaluation strategies and systems. There is also an allocation in this grant for wellness in furtherance of the organization&#x2019;s charitable purpose. (Strategy: Inclusive Governance)</narrative>
  </description>
